    "turn_text": "From the New York Times, I'm Michael Bobaro. This is Daily. Today. Days after moderate House Democrats announced they would support an impeachment inquiry against President Trump, they returned home to their swing districts on recess. It's the first time they faced their constituents since that decision. Congresswoman Alyssa Slotkin of Michigan went to three town halls last week. We went with her to all of them. It's Wednesday, October 9th. Congressman, I'd love for you to go back to a couple of weeks ago. You're headed home to your district in Michigan for the first time since you've made this decision that you surely knew would upset many of your constituents. Was there any question in your mind whether you would hold town halls while you were back in your district?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_08",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
