    "turn_text": "I was surprised that people thought that that was okay. And I tried to give the example in Heartland that, hey, today it could be a Republican president reaching out to Ukraine. Tomorrow it could be a Democratic president reaching out to China. I think it has more of an impact on people because Ukraine might be difficult for folks to understand, especially since they're a partner nation. But I think most people in Michigan understand that reaching out to China would be a bad thing. But by the time I got out of the town hall, the president had suggested that.",
